@{b}                         ZAPPHelper v1.1@{ub}
                        By Andrew Herbert

  Welcome to ZAPPHelper, the following information will allow you to setup
  ZAPPHelper on your Zeus BBS system providing you already have the Zeus
  Asyncronous Packet Protocol (ZAPP) installed.  ZAPPHelper also requires
  reqtools to operate.

 @{" What does ZAPPHelper do?  " Link "What" }
 @{" Command Line Operation    " Link "Command" }
 @{" Docking ZAPPHelper        " Link "Dock" }

 @{" Help!                     " Link "Help" }

 @{" Version History           " Link "Version" }

  ZAPPHelper is FreeWare and may be freely distributed.
@endnode

@Node "What" "What does ZAPPHelper do?"

@{b}                         What does ZAPPHelper do?@{ub}


  ZAPPHelper provides simple host operation of the Zeus Asyncronous Packet
  Protocol by providing GUI controls to its currently available operations.
  Whilst running ZAPPHelper will appear on Workbench as a icon or a "virtual
  device", by dragging and dropping files, drawers or devices on this icon
  you will be able to send or play files or even mount drawers or whole
  devices.  By double clicking on the icon you will be able to send messages
  and view ZAPPStatus information using a Magic Workbench icon toolbar.

  Make sure you have ZAPPHelper.info in the same directory as ZAPPHelper
  otherwise no icon will appear on your Workbench.
@endnode

@node "Command" "Command Line Operation"

@{b}                         Command Line Operation@{ub}


  To use ZAPPHelper just use the simple command:

              ZAPPHelper <line number> or
              ZAPPHelper LINE <line number>

  ZAPPHelper will then check if Zeus is running, then if the desired line
  is active and finally whether ZAPPHelper is already runnning on that
  line.  If any of these events are true ZAPPHelper will terminate giving
  an appropriate error message.

  Make sure you have ZAPPHelper.info in the same directory as ZAPPHelper
  otherwise no icon will appear on your Workbench.
@endnode

@node "Dock" "Docking ZAPPHelper"

@{b}                         Docking ZAPPHelper@{ub}

  For the purpose of this mini-tutorial you are required to put ZAPPHelper
  in Zeus:Bin.

  By docking ZAPPHelper you can have a shortcut to ZAPPHelper on your Zeus
  screen at all times.  To dock ZAPPHelper make sure you've installed the
  ZAPPHelper dock icon in Zeus:Config/Icons and run Zeus:Prefs/DockCFG.  To
  add a dock click on the Add gadget and type "ZAPPHelper" now go to the
  Execute string gadget and type "Zeus:Bin/ZAPPHelper <Line>" where line is
  the numeric value of you first serial line (normally this is 1).  Now go
  to the Text String Gadget and type "ZAPP <Line>" and finally Save then
  Update.

  You should now have a ZAPPHelper dock icon on your zeus screen which when
  clicked will allow you to mount devices, drawers or send and play files
  over your serial line.  To move the dockicon go back into
  Zeus:Prefs/DockCFG and use the FindPos Gadget.

  Make sure you have ZAPPHelper.info in the same directory as ZAPPHelper
  otherwise no icon will appear on your Workbench.
@endnode

@node "Help" "Help!"

@{b}                         Help!@{ub}


  Q: The ZAPPHelper icon doesn't appear on my Workbench!?
  A: ZAPPHelper requires its .info file "ZAPPHelper.info" in the same
     directory as ZAPPHelper.

  Q: ZAPPStatus returns the information on line 0 only!?
  A: Yep, it sure does! :)  This is a problem with ZAPPStatus itself.

  Q: I'm getting constant "Please Insert Volume ZAPP:" requesters.
  A: Assign ZAPP: as Zeus:Bin/ZAPP/

  Q: My Hard Disk has been formatted and I've got a great big picture of a
     cow on my screen.
  A: This will happen every Monday between the hours of 6pm-7pm if
     ZAPPHelper is still running.
@endnode

